    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Probability</p>
    <h1>Are Dice Rolls Really Random? How Fair Randomness Works</h1>
    <p class="lead">A fair die gives each face the same chance on every roll, and the rolls do not depend on each other. Computers imitate this with random number generators, and the quality of that generator decides whether the results are fair.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>What fair means</h2>
<p>A fair six-sided die should show each face about one time in six over many rolls. The outcome of one roll should not change the odds for the next.</p>
<h2>Why a simple approach can be biased</h2>
<p>Taking a random number and using the remainder after dividing by the number of sides can favour some faces, if the range does not divide evenly. A fair generator discards the few values that would cause this, so every face has the same chance.</p>
<h2>Secure random numbers</h2>
<p>The dice roller uses the browser's cryptographic random source, and it applies this rejection step. That makes the results suitable for games and fair draws, though not a substitute for a physical die in a formal competition.</p>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>The <a href="/tools/dice-roller.html">Dice Roller</a> rolls up to twenty dice with 4 to 100 sides, and shows each result and the total.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>Roll two six-sided dice. There are 36 equally likely pairs. Only six pairs add up to 7 (1+6, 2+5, 3+4, 4+3, 5+2, 6+1), so a total of 7 comes up in 6 out of 36 rolls, about 17%. A total of 2 comes up only once in 36, which is about 3%.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Why does 7 come up more often than 2 with two dice?</summary><p>There are more pairs of faces that add up to 7 than to any other total. A total of 2 can only be made by rolling two 1s.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is a dice roller on a website fair?</summary><p>It is fair if the random source is unbiased and every face is equally likely. The Dice Roller uses the browser's secure random numbers and avoids the bias that a simple remainder calculation can cause.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I use a dice roller for real money bets?</summary><p>Check the rules that apply where you live and to the game. Online tools are useful for games and decisions, but they are not a substitute for a regulated gambling service.</p></details>
      </section>
